# UI Architecture & Design System

- **Framework**: Next.js 16 (App Router), `output: 'export'` — static, no runtime server.
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4. All tokens live in `app/globals.css`.
- **Animations**: Framer Motion for scroll reveals; CSS `animation-delay` for the
  page-load sequence. Everything respects `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Theming**: both light and dark must work, via `next-themes` (class strategy).
  Never hardcode a colour — read `--primary`, `--card`, `--border`, `--ok`/`--warn`/`--err`.
  The accent differs per theme, so a literal hex will be wrong in one of them.
- **Design**: "control room" — deep desaturated purple-graphite base, glass panels
  with real elevation, one cyan-teal accent. Full rules and the reasoning behind
  them are in `.agents/skills/premium-portfolio-ui/SKILL.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- **Components**: bespoke and lean. The dependency list went 47 → 9 deliberately;
  `@radix-ui/react-dialog` is the only UI library left. Do not add a component
  library back.
- **Content**: never hardcode copy in a component. Everything comes from
  `content/{profile,experience,projects,skills,writing}.ts`.
